    "dm_scale_invariance_note": "5%/10%/20% BTC have identical DM t-stats because d_10=2*d_5, d_20=4*d_5. The DM t-statistic is scale-invariant: t(c*d) = c*mean/(c*std/sqrt(n)) = t(d). This means DM tests whether BTC adds significant return, but cannot distinguish optimal allocation size. The 5% vs 10% vs 20% choice is purely risk-preference.",
